  ('66b6dd88-9575-55d2-bd4b-7326ae16e528', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'The critical developmental assignment for an MOS 92M Staff Sergeant as a Section Chief for 24 months or serving on staff for 24 months. Although the proponent recommends all MOS 92M Staff Sergeants serve a minimum of 24 months as a Section Chief prior to being assigned to other leadership duties in operational units, unit strengths, operational requirements, and unit priorities may require Commanders and Command Sergeant Majors to move Staff Sergeants prior to meeting this requirement. Assignments in Operational Army units as a Fatality Management NCO and Section Chief.', '0b2baca46407e25c9870a36a8505a9e2f971e7bb4896886e0288c04ad98ea303', 26, 26, null, 183, null, null, false, null),
  ('1fc0ea5a-231a-53ce-90ff-2238708b830b', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'Staff Sergeants selected for TDA gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These tours should be limited to one (1) three-year tour, except for those personnel required to complete a broadening tour in support of Army requirement. TDA assignments include ALC Instructor, Instructor, Fatality Management OC, Fatality Management NCO, Recovery Supervisor, Recruiter, and Senior Fatality Management NCO.', 'ead51b437f958fbf69f05033765d2795083c84b6dc4a065cf11232a35682b386', 26, 26, null, 184, null, null, false, null),
  ('6b8b4e6a-d375-58e8-a747-28163e82d60b', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-Development', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to chapter 3; Army Career Tracker (ACT) at https://actnow.army.mil; TC 7-22.7; Army Training Information System (ATIS) at https://www.pdmatis.army.mil/', '515f219fb8e169a536b2385da6b4b99e2c10f1e12bc930b9951996b218903d5c', 26, 26, null, 185, null, null, false, null),
  ('4121a86b-f64c-5408-84c8-4249914a2c3a', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional Training', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'Airborne, Jumpmaster, Air Assault, Ranger, Battle Staff, Master Driver Trainer, Master Resiliency Trainer Facilitator, Equal Opportunity Leader, Master Fitness Trainer, HAZMAT Course, Contracting Officer Representative (COR), Support Operations Course, Sling Load Inspector Certification Course (SLICC), and Enlisted Aide Training Course.', 'd28a97140d40b0980a0e65935d4694b4d044dfd1c86158361437ea524c9aef48', 26, 26, null, 186, null, null, false, null),
  ('84e30e9c-b96d-5ba2-bdd4-5f78ca1849e8', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', '1) Broadening Assignments: Instructor, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Enlisted Aide, and Congressional Fellowship. 2) MOS Enhancing: Special Mission Units, or Special Operations assignments.', 'f7b3a832da3d937f2638ece4b412f57d6695b2708365d7c97b3d092af5fb6979', 26, 26, null, 187, null, null, false, null),
  ('261000c5-2cf4-5a6e-b91a-cc3e4a8d0ea8', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional training', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'MLC, Master Resiliency Trainer Level 2, and Reclassification.', 'b0103ba5f969fd2b456bffe62a96f113257cbcb4328ddc44cc047d32f96595ca', 26, 26, null, 188, null, null, false, null),
  ('58901d98-df7d-5aca-9f46-9c42b94872a6', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'The critical developmental assignment for an MOS 92M Sergeant First Class as a Platoon Sergeant for 24 months or serving on staff for 18-23 months. Although the proponent recommends all MOS 92M Sergeant First Class’s serve a minimum of 24 months as a Platoon Sergeant or on staff prior to being assigned to other leadership duties in operational units, unit strengths, operational requirements, and unit priorities may require Commanders and Command Sergeant Majors to move Sergeant First Class’s prior to meeting this requirement. Assignments in Operational Army units as a Fatality Management NCO, Platoon Sergeant, and Senior Fatality Management NCO.', '798ba86ec7761ddf5b2a662f38f5289f3a910043071ebb76a98611898805c45d', 27, 27, null, 189, null, null, false, null),
  ('5ffb9fa4-6d18-575f-85ea-495232dee77e', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'Sergeant First Class’s selected for TDA gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the Operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These should be limited to one (1) three-year tour, with the exception of those personnel required to complete a broadening tour in support of Army requirement. TDA assignments include BSB Fatality Management NCO OC/T, Instructor, Fatality Management NCO, PLOPS NCO, SCI Analysis NCOIC, Section NCO, and Trainer Developer.', '7d242748dda0cbee9295cc72d87320d98cc44784e433b0030648a154ff62c573', 27, 27, null, 190, null, null, false, null),
  ('d73448cb-f8e2-5fa3-80d6-b44f9ae64b78', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-Development', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to chapter 3; Army Career Tracker (ACT) at https://actnow.army.mil; TC 7-22.7; Army Training Information System (ATIS) at https://www.pdmatis.army.mil/.', '7345beb1d9eab7bc9ff4d40e11cfed7f7dc794420c71074b13e9a2d06abd0275', 27, 27, null, 191, null, null, false, null),
  ('a26ffef1-7ded-52cc-9de5-3bd289b2c88d', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional Training', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'Airborne, Jumpmaster, Air Assault, Ranger, Battle Staff, Master Driver Trainer, Master Resiliency Trainer, Master Fitness Trainer, HAZMAT Course, Contracting Officer Representative (COR), Master Resilience Trainer- Assistant Primary Instructor, Support Operations Course, and Sling Load Inspector Certification Course (SLICC), and Enlisted Aide Training Course.', '1025318b526f0c394f07b3e6db0192480da1f27b3d7e9127cf79bb85a0fdd7dc', 27, 27, null, 192, null, null, false, null),
  ('c6ff83d1-8128-579e-800a-e69f05b2ba7f', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Special assignments', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', '1) Broadening Assignments: Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Instructor, SLC Senior Small Group Leader, Inspector General, Career Management NCO, Equal Opportunity Advisor, Enlisted Aide, Congressional Fellowship, and Talent Management NCO. 2) MOS Enhancing: Special Mission Units, or Special Operations assignments.', '3f314c9f89602a1ebb6fe52c68213ed29eaccd7c487e71b0c7fbf8f4c101afa0', 27, 27, null, 193, null, null, false, null),
  ('8cd4ae03-c6d5-52c5-9b2c-bd7b8a281543', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'SGM-A', '9dd76cebaa7df888b4fa51b65c80bd2c31219d93a2969295e38d1a4de0e16af9', 27, 27, null, 194, null, null, false, null),
  ('3ba2d499-b2b8-53a7-89af-51932b85950d', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'Assignments in Operational Army units as a First Sergeant and Senior Fatality Management NCO. Critical Development time for leadership positions will be 24 months. For all staff positions, Critical Development time will be 18-36 months.', 'aadc8015c52b9fd7ebd2bcb7e4f0e8edfb415d16779ffa702b79560f6cc8f662', 27, 27, null, 195, null, null, false, null),
  ('fc6e5bbf-53f1-5a56-8a1f-178e1d5d8069', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'Master Sergeants selected for TDA gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These tours should be limited to one (1) three-year tour, except for those personnel required to complete a broadening tour in support of Army requirements. TDA assignments include Course Manager, Chief Instructor, Operations SGT, and Worldwide OPS NCOIC.', '17e94cc3dd11971f81b225a9611e145a30ff234c377251e928c96df608f8a0f1', 27, 27, null, 196, null, null, false, null),
  ('08302d3e-c841-582c-82af-b8601c50badf', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Self-Development', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to chapter 3; Army Career Tracker (ACT) at https://actnow.army.mil; TC 7-22.7; Army Training Information System (ATIS) at https://www.pdmatis.army.mil/.', '7345beb1d9eab7bc9ff4d40e11cfed7f7dc794420c71074b13e9a2d06abd0275', 27, 27, null, 197, null, null, false, null),
  ('33da0aed-cebf-51e8-b3ef-4bc3c091174c', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Additional Training', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'Airborne, Jumpmaster, Air Assault, Ranger, HAZMAT course, Battle Staff, Master Resiliency Trainer, Master Fitness Trainer, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response and Prevention (SHARP), Equal Opportunity Advisor, Inspector General, Support Operations Course, Joint Logistics Course, and Enlisted Aide Training Course.', 'e8cd2d02c29cfe2401a74417e7bd25ea038a6bfc7676df4f90d409e5933efee6', 27, 27, null, 198, null, null, false, null),
  ('4ac43db0-a2e9-539c-984d-8e92d8a7efdc', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', '1) Broadening Assignments: Congressional Fellowship and Enlisted Aide. 2) MOS Enhancing: Ranger Battalion, Security Force Assistance Brigade (SFAB), Special Mission Units, or Special Operations assignments.', '785b2c2e77a22348b3fb266e9ce31c3a1cf3434049767f3495c7b1466bdef680', 27, 27, null, 199, null, null, false, null),
  ('195863b7-9321-53dd-b639-a0f41356f1a3', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92M', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major — overview', 'Chapter 16. MOS 92M Mortuary Affairs Specialist/Fatality Management Specialist', 'Sergeant Majors/Command Sergeant Majors with the MOS 92A, 92Y,92F, 92G, 92M, 92R, and 92S convert to MOS 92Z, Senior Noncommissioned Logistician, See section 10-92Z. MOS 92Z—Senior Noncommissioned Logistician, CMF 92 within Smartbook DA Pam 611-21 located at https://www.milsuite.mil/.', 'd84bb937819d1fe4087b8d71a1db1541a57b55cc39a2d7d2471016b86ccd538a', 27, 27, null, 200, null, null, false, null),
  ('31c344d9-9d55-57b7-8c22-4fca7f39949c', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'The Parachute Rigger must focus and become proficient in the skills of their MOS and continue to broaden their knowledge to positively affect their careers. The Parachute Rigger should become a Jumpmaster (5W) by the rank of Staff Sergeant which is critical to the overall success, health, and readiness of the Rigger Military Occupational Specialty. Warrior Tasks and Battle Drills cannot be overlooked; the Quartermaster Soldier should have the tactical skills needed to survive on the battlefield and strive for excellence during the ACFT and weapons qualification.', '9ee25b4e2163262ebe80ce125c0026c71baacccb3896db50c9c9b07bcca23b1f', 28, 28, null, 201, null, null, false, null),
  ('b62a9829-e899-50a0-9f93-7990e8320dc6', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'IET, Reclassification training, and BLC.', '0cac5d92a181099ea2e7459ab7b4aebe0ee0f8e6654aa905564fa46aacab73de', 28, 28, null, 202, null, null, false, null),
  ('0f8e4932-87f9-59b4-952a-2030f6182aba', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'Assignments in Operational Army units as an Airdrop Equipment Repair Specialist, Parachute Packer/Airdrop Specialist, Parachute Packer, Vehicle Operator, Airdrop Specialist, Air Items Control Specialist, and Airdrop Ops Specialist.', '5d14fb0bcda03068307339d30fbc16b9749d26a669c5ea9411bdd9be17cb6652', 28, 28, null, 203, null, null, false, null),
  ('6c573eb5-423d-50b5-81c6-2a026677e96d', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'Soldiers selected for TDA gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These tours should be limited to one (1) three-year tour. TDA assignments include Parachute Pack, Airdrop Eq RPR, Parachute Packer.', '105892a950756cd9f0ac829c87884e57ee5919f65d6ca11780e954527b2ddd1d', 28, 28, null, 204, null, null, false, null),
  ('c50660d7-52ed-5cd5-a176-bc05a3edb1cd', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to chapter 3; Army Career Tracker (ACT) at https://actnow.army.mil; TC 7-22.7; Army Training Information System (ATIS) at https://www.pdmatis.army.mil/.', '7345beb1d9eab7bc9ff4d40e11cfed7f7dc794420c71074b13e9a2d06abd0275', 28, 28, null, 205, null, null, false, null),
  ('b9f9334e-d2d7-56b1-8c3a-1c9e4ea476f7', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Additional Training', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'Combatives 1, Combat Lifesaver, Field Sanitation, Airborne, Air Assault, and Ranger.', '045104a8d240b67595ac31743064d7d55fa166560cc0712caf171d162ee93fd1', 28, 28, null, 206, null, null, false, null),
  ('08dc03a6-2871-53e7-b146-1712a9bc7449', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Special assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', '1) Broadening Assignments: None.
(2) MOS Enhancing: Ranger Battalion or Special Operations assignments.', 'dc423dc55eaae98ae88cf617b9ed966f96c663e96a45e971feecea128a53edb7', 29, 29, null, 207, null, null, false, null),
  ('23ede9ea-1543-520f-b221-178c79375a4e', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'ALC and Reclassification.', 'cf63d356c621c858c25193d29febe2bcb14d92ae16c3f8e8fcc8fd8e148accdf', 29, 29, null, 208, null, null, false, null),
  ('300d41fb-7c9f-54af-8c5d-b7883948121f', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'The critical developmental assignment for an MOS 92R Sergeant as a Squad Leader for 12 months. Although the proponent recommends all MOS 92R Sergeants serve a minimum of 12 months as a Squad Leader prior to being assigned to other leadership duties in operational units, unit strengths, operational requirements, and unit priorities may require Commanders and Command Sergeant Majors to move Sergeants prior to meeting this requirement. Assignments in Operational Army units as a Parachute Packer, Inspector/Tester, Airdrop/Equipment Repair SGT, In Process Inspector, Air Items Control SGT, Final Pack Inspector, and Airdrop SGT.', '285cfa375b58ec31df97b6498ed44b2232769d22d4b4df680a6b0cf1cc2115d3', 29, 29, null, 209, null, null, false, null),
  ('e331d8f4-3fb3-5986-a604-44278abd25c7', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'Sergeants selected for TDA gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These tours should be limited to one (1) three-year tour, with the exception of those personnel required to complete a broadening tour in support of Army requirement. TDA assignments include Drill Sergeant or Instructor, Inspector Tester, Parachute Packer, Rigger NCO, Airdrop Equipment Repair Supervisor.', '48c719fee5b2fc50e821642d7ef3ed79a0d5f86a37a3dc00a7b0b6e86485037e', 29, 29, null, 210, null, null, false, null),
  ('5e1d1db7-dbb2-5f54-91f4-d1cb5139687d', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to chapter 3; Army Career Tracker (ACT) at https://actnow.army.mil; TC 7-22.7; Army Training Information System (ATIS) at https://www.pdmatis.army.mil/.', '7345beb1d9eab7bc9ff4d40e11cfed7f7dc794420c71074b13e9a2d06abd0275', 29, 29, null, 211, null, null, false, null),
  ('04e61328-3af8-555e-9f56-d38b8a144c45', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'Additional training, Airborne, Jumpmaster, Air Assault, Ranger, Master Driver Trainer, Enlisted Aide Training Course, Master Resiliency Trainer, Master Fitness Trainer, HAZMAT Course, Sling Load Inspector Certification Course (SLICC), Inspector Course, Airdrop Load Inspector Course (ALICC), Military Free Fall (MFF), Military Free Fall Jumpmaster, Pathfinder and Field Sanitation.', 'f3cf6c99bff766f5415786db368afbb4cf5408cc3896557245b264e8d5bface0', 29, 29, null, 212, null, null, false, null),
  ('f2962bc2-b3ae-5690-a6fd-49e9bbd1d2c5', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', '1) Broadening Assignments: Recruiter, Drill Sergeant, Enlisted Aide and Test Jumper. 2) MOS Enhancing: Ranger Battalion, Special Mission Units, or Special Operations assignments.', '2c74bc85e7b41cc002d1ceb596067a4fab1fbdcc6d75b4ad2f0b685fee78714e', 29, 29, null, 213, null, null, false, null),
  ('9ac2d22b-92f6-5734-a261-62bf0e8077b2', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'SLC and Reclassification.', '89465a136a1bc1d444b6ef3a5cb30f668f135a6ec2e7ca121e3e36965ce77e32', 29, 29, null, 214, null, null, false, null),
  ('5ee609a1-3a47-566e-8cf3-aabdb1efdf37', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'The critical developmental assignment for an MOS 92R Staff Sergeant as a Squad Leader/Section Sergeant for 24 months or serving on staff for 24 months. Although the proponent recommends all MOS 92R Staff Sergeants serve a minimum of 24 months as a Squad Leader/Section Sergeant or First Sergeant 18-24 months prior to being assigned to other leadership duties in operational units, unit strengths, operational requirements, and unit priorities may require Commanders and Command Sergeant Majors to move Staff Sergeants prior to meeting this requirement. Assignments in Operational Army units as a Squad Leader, Shop Foreman, Air Items Control SGT, Airdrop Supervisor, Parachute Packer Supervisor, and Section Chief.', 'b0058df6087b02f91af9e08ce4d01ccf4d6ec73e34647aefe01a683478864948', 29, 29, null, 215, null, null, false, null),
  ('bcd1c2a2-6e13-593a-814b-a5ed25c43bf6', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'Staff Sergeants selected for TDA gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These tours should be limited to one (1) three- year tour, except for those personnel required to complete a broadening tour in support of Army requirement. TDA assignments include Drill Sergeant, Instructor/Writer, Training Developer, Career Manager, Airdrop Equip Rep Supervisor, Parachute Packer Supervisor, Inspector Tester Supervisor, HC Para-Rigger, Airdrop Supervisor, Parachutist, Recruiter, Operations SGT, ALC SGL, and Training SGT.', '885f57a04380fc1a2fc1c1fd98c07500aa4d47171f6e31bcae089c0ceedfcfd0', 29, 29, null, 216, null, null, false, null),
  ('0f446b70-e0f3-5e6c-966e-db695cf5538d', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-Development', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to chapter 3; Army Career Tracker (ACT) at https://actnow.army.mil; TC 7-22.7; Army Training Information System (ATIS) at https://www.pdmatis.army.mil/.', '7345beb1d9eab7bc9ff4d40e11cfed7f7dc794420c71074b13e9a2d06abd0275', 29, 29, null, 217, null, null, false, null),
  ('3d1df1b7-8f75-5e9a-83ee-3fc8c27cb6e8', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional Training', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'Sling Load Inspector Certification Course (SLICC)., Airdrop Load Inspector Certification Course, Air Assault, Ranger, Contracting Officer Representative (COR), Support Operations Course, and Battle Staff Course, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response Prevention (SHARP), Jumpmaster, Military Free Fall (MFF), Military Free Fall Jumpmaster, Pathfinder and Enlisted Aide Training Course.', '86a7b8a27aeaacb97c24d997e099f29313d324e1dd5e3298764dd090b03acf46', 30, 30, null, 218, null, null, false, null),
  ('860e2dc7-021c-5ce6-93d1-f7c1a3609959', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', '1) Broadening Assignments: Competitive Parachutist, Test Jumper, Instructor, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Small Group Leader, Enlisted Aide, and Test Directorate Fort Bragg & YPG. 2) MOS Enhancing: Security Force Assistance Brigade (SFAB), Ranger Battalion, Special Mission Units, or Special Operations assignments.', 'c8f23fc419f25715d97d8a2a8ce4ac2fd8b66c72fc06fbf4c9ed89bcaa65d1c2', 30, 30, null, 219, null, null, false, null),
  ('95174940-f252-5686-87e7-ada762658867', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional training', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'MLC and Reclassification.', 'ed9311ac4790ece28b2d6195d74ee44e265d355c90ab296c515eecc651806c43', 30, 30, null, 220, null, null, false, null),
  ('2ac28b4e-92c7-5bd0-8c5c-b4fe2002b126', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'The critical developmental assignment for an MOS 92R Sergeant First Class as a Platoon Sergeant or serving on staff for 24 months. Although the proponent recommends all MOS 92R Sergeant First Class’s serve a minimum of 24 months as a Platoon Sergeant or on staff prior to being assigned to other leadership duties in operational units, unit strengths, operational requirements, and unit priorities may require Commanders and Command Sergeant Majors to move Sergeant First Class’s prior to meeting this requirement. Assignments in Operational Army units as a Platoon Sergeant, Airdrop Equipment NCO, Parachute Packer Supervisor, and Airdrop OPS NCO.', '495454ca086f3b0578f4e452aef4e57beb468687e9aabc602be2c3b688b2ad35', 30, 30, null, 221, null, null, false, null),
  ('13c10318-6abc-5258-8b34-d4c4a71d5127', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'Sergeant First Class’s selected for TDA gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These tours should be limited to one three-year tour, with the exception of those personnel required to complete a broadening tour in support of Army requirement such as Drill Sergeant, Instructor, Airdrop Eq NCO, Airdrop OPS NCO, NCOIC Air Delivery Div, Rigger NCOIC, HC SR Parachute Rigger, Air Delivery NCO, ADE Rep Supervisor, Supervisor SR Parachute Rigger, Supervisor MFF Para packer, CMP Parachutist, Tandem Parachutist, Training Dev, Operations SGT, SR Airdrop OPS Supervisor, SLC SGL.', '3ef44ff4aebc58e4c05dd6336eab2cb75d176180a3e6af38c4c26a1e2729ca29', 30, 30, null, 222, null, null, false, null),
  ('cc7d2b51-ea25-5fbc-b953-bc332f627d9a', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-Development', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to chapter 3; Army Career Tracker (ACT) at https://actnow.army.mil; TC 7-22.7; Army Training Information System (ATIS) at https://www.pdmatis.army.mil/.', '7345beb1d9eab7bc9ff4d40e11cfed7f7dc794420c71074b13e9a2d06abd0275', 30, 30, null, 223, null, null, false, null),
  ('abf8cb67-5772-52dc-b7bb-4a724d2b479f', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional Training', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', ', Airborne, Jumpmaster, Air Assault, Ranger, Master Fitness Trainer, Master Driver Trainer, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response and Prevention (SHARP), Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA), HAZMAT, Battle Staff, Sling Load Inspector Certification Course (SLICC),, Support Operations Course, Joint Logistics Course, Contracting Officer Representative (COR), Master Resilience Trainer-Assistant Primary Instructor, Military Free Fall (MFF), Military Free Fall Jumpmaster, Pathfinder, and Enlisted Aide Training Course.', '288b30a434310316e92ded109a04b9031da64951fde29f688dd924d3c6b0147f', 30, 30, null, 224, null, null, false, null),
  ('b37acf90-58cf-539b-97ca-c920c740f243', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Special assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', '1) Broadening Assignments: Test Jumper, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Instructor, Senior Small Group Leader, Enlisted Aide, Inspector General, Career Management NCO, Equal Opportunity Advisor, Talent Management NCO, and Training Developer. 2) MOS Enhancing: Security Force Assistance Brigade (SFAB), Ranger Battalion, Special Mission Units, or Special Operations assignments.', 'e52a420b786fe576d70c454c53790bd85cc389f5dfcdbc96b6fa936ffc501935', 30, 30, null, 225, null, null, false, null),
  ('27dee309-5c99-5f76-ba83-a65aba5faaee', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army career degrees', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'See SOCAD Army Career Degree Program. (h) GI to Jobs. See GI to Jobs COOL Website.', '89f2722b644654d6c57e608adaf80936b7cdc1a68cce9de47fce169e6f739fa1', 30, 30, null, 226, null, null, false, null),
  ('de3da372-3d15-5259-ac4f-3ded1e3d84b7', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'SGM-A', '9dd76cebaa7df888b4fa51b65c80bd2c31219d93a2969295e38d1a4de0e16af9', 30, 30, null, 227, null, null, false, null),
  ('3ad3ab3e-e0df-50e6-baf5-43bc0114da7f', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'Critical Development time for leadership positions will be 24 months. For all staff positions, Critical Development time will be 24 Months. Assignments in Operational Army as a First Sergeant and Senior Airdrop Operations NCO 24 months', '6f0297071177c8908a1e4945f33361eaa96669bfe36b4a63bed38f40bf747372', 30, 30, null, 228, null, null, false, null),
  ('d80e3bd6-5cbd-5646-b98b-b52c3ff99000', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'Master Sergeants selected for TDA gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These tours should be limited to one (1) three-year tour, with the exception of those personnel required to complete a broadening tour in support of Army requirement. TDA assignments include Chief Instructor, Senior Instructor (CRS MGR), SR Airdrop OPS NCO, SR AD EQNCO Tester, SR Airdrop NCO/ TP, SR Airdrop OPS Supervisor, First Sergeant, and SR Airdrop Equip NCO.', '70b05858168d749b6fe7e83b0dc3bb0e626c6f52cd3f3cb01889902125143e90', 31, 31, null, 229, null, null, false, null),
