(f) GI to Jobs. See GI to Jobs COOL Website.', 'd380e2fae4677aaf8bb4a414b4c0f71a2053359972b1a909988b1b147a1fab24', 31, 31, null, 233, null, null, false, null),
  ('453f5d60-0a1d-5fa9-b77f-832478432aa2', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major — overview', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'Sergeant Majors/Command Sergeant Majors with the MOS 92A, 92Y,92F, 92G, 92M, 92R, and 92S convert to MOS 92Z, Senior Noncommissioned Logistician, See section 10-92Z. MOS 92Z—Senior Noncommissioned Logistician, CMF 92 within Smartbook DA Pam 611-21 located at https://www.milsuite.mil/.', 'd84bb937819d1fe4087b8d71a1db1541a57b55cc39a2d7d2471016b86ccd538a', 31, 31, null, 234, null, null, false, null),
  ('3965e887-dfec-5dda-9716-a986df74bb31', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'Shower and Laundry Specialists must focus and become proficient in the skill of their MOS and continue to broaden their knowledge that will in turn reflect on them positively later in their careers. Warrior Tasks and Battle Drills cannot be overlooked; the Quartermaster Soldier should enhance the tactical skills needed to survive on the battlefield and strive for excellence during the ACFT and weapons qualification.', 'ea0c0d13400da094e565d078b139fe571f6b057ec4fc1589afb3c374ad94fde6', 32, 32, null, 235, null, null, false, null),
  ('8f951d54-26b2-5d94-91e5-0e5228a07bbe', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'IET, Reclassification, BLC.', 'c6928b19702683dec69a36de32ae85d8c7df282809988d9e3ce2afcebaa88215', 32, 32, null, 236, null, null, false, null),
