  ('862cec00-34db-5d87-a6a7-df4e95cfe293', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92W', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Special assignments', 'Chapter 25. MOS 92W Water Treatment Specialist', '1) Broadening Assignments: Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Enlisted Aide, Inspector General, Talent Management NCO, Career Management NCO, Equal Opportunity Advisor, Observer/Controller Trainer (OCT), Instructor, Senior Small Group Leader 2) MOS Enhancing: Any Special Operations assignment.', 'b7b2f7112000c0f923341347d493b3d854e2a7e0386d423aee271bd6541929e0', 37, 37, null, 289, null, null, false, null),
  ('f19938f6-9052-50f0-953b-e7d7c69431bc', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92W', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army career degrees', 'Chapter 25. MOS 92W Water Treatment Specialist', 'See SOCAD Army Career Degree Program. (h) GI to Jobs. See GI to Jobs COOL Website', '9b037f90ce61bfe5ea7a65ed9cdd62f156b7008f2a53bb0bc117e6da1107b769', 37, 37, null, 290, null, null, false, null),
  ('3ad36728-dd1b-5c00-b202-8e2c03919f0f', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92W', null, 'development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Additional guidance', 'Chapter 25. MOS 92W Water Treatment Specialist', 'All MOS 92W convert to MOS 92F, Petroleum Supply Specialist at the rank of Master Sergeant. See para 29-7 for additional information.', '7da1e62642ea8eec82d1049e85cfd1451c18aa2d9e073523890d56ea72cc9343', 37, 37, null, 291, null, null, false, null),
  ('f1cde18d-8389-5197-a212-650dff571cc2', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92W', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major — overview', 'Chapter 25. MOS 92W Water Treatment Specialist', 'Sergeant Majors/Command Sergeant Majors with the MOS 92A, 92Y,92F, 92G, 92M, 92R, and 92S convert to MOS 92Z, Senior Noncommissioned Logistician, See section 10-92Z. MOS 92Z—Senior Noncommissioned Logistician, CMF 92 within Smartbook DA Pam 611-21 located at https://www.milsuite.mil/.', 'd84bb937819d1fe4087b8d71a1db1541a57b55cc39a2d7d2471016b86ccd538a', 37, 37, null, 292, null, null, false, null),
  ('1a5c0712-da0e-5cfc-b234-e1e113c07a1c', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'Unit Supply Specialist must focus and become proficient in the skills of their MOS and continue to broaden their knowledge that will in turn reflect on them positively later in their careers. Warrior Tasks and Battle Drills cannot be overlooked; the Quartermaster Soldier should enhance the tactical skills needed to survive on the battlefield and strive for excellence during the ACFT and weapons qualification.', '618a67d3574bf0866a16ba2fa36ecadd34c8220013a08256f1227ae2bc25fd1e', 38, 38, null, 293, null, null, false, null),
  ('c20d25a9-a45a-5fa7-9a2c-76bd18eaa45d', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'IET, Reclassification, and BLC.', '3eabfa175c4c11850585ad1a19dfa95d1f3612089f88bd928e8c5cce18e95082', 38, 38, null, 294, null, null, false, null),
  ('e651b4f6-73d9-5930-84b4-1cbc174d772e', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'Assignments in Operational Army units as a Unit Supply Specialist, Vehicle Operator, and Property Book Specialist.', '34faa3ab7f1838f824aa0eb8c946effa3fe6ef161eff42eb8bfe01ad1eae61d8', 38, 38, null, 295, null, null, false, null),
  ('8c6a4b6a-6244-5d8a-8dac-a20511f02a4b', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'Soldiers selected for TDA assignments gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These tours should be limited to one three- year tour. TDA assignments include Supply Specialist, Armorer, Field Supt Spec, Supply Clerk, Admin Training Specialist, Property SP, Ammo Support, and Vehicle Driver.', 'f08ba572a133d59da83732c632941125100d5f95b1a17af923ba944b6d55e1ee', 38, 39, null, 296, null, null, false, null),
  ('969e7bea-021d-5712-959b-161688ac5e7d', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Self-development', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to chapter 3; Army Career Tracker (ACT) at https://actnow.army.mil; TC 7-22.7; Army Training Information System (ATIS) at https://www.pdmatis.army.mil/.', '7345beb1d9eab7bc9ff4d40e11cfed7f7dc794420c71074b13e9a2d06abd0275', 39, 39, null, 297, null, null, false, null),
  ('337c8b51-cc27-5315-a877-c982f4350caf', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Additional Training', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'Airborne, Air Assault, Ranger, HAZMAT Course, Combatives, Comabt Life Savers, Field Sanitation, GCSS-Army Material Managers Course, and Sling Load Inspector Certification Course (SLICC).', 'fb14993c9bd9612d29147879b4d9019e2a90bb92fb3a5ee56b182f28cf615a6b', 39, 39, null, 298, null, null, false, null),
  ('0f6f99cb-f53a-559c-9c91-b967e3d5b90d', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Special assignments', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', '1) Broadening Assignments: None. 2) MOS Enhancing: Special Mission Units, Ranger Battalion, White House Communications Agency (WHCA), or Special Operations.', '76b7e9604e3f6bd53fb7027217c59fe0e431e2c0469041e81be256ada4e12420', 39, 39, null, 299, null, null, false, null),
  ('2726a1ff-fda9-50b7-b6e5-1b5d954c40cc', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'ALC, and Reclassification.', '99e4a03b5fb8659059a8a19e1ce05dc0c7a20317e25f0f32ac722f1cee0fc896', 39, 39, null, 300, null, null, false, null),
  ('1612205c-1bce-5209-b65d-ee3b19c254f0', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'The critical developmental assignment for an MOS 92Y Sergeant as a Team/Squad Leader for 24 months or serving on staff for 18-24 months. Although the proponent recommends all MOS 92YSergeants serve a minimum of 24 months as a Team/Squad Leader prior to being assigned to other leadership duties in operational units, unit strengths, operational requirements, and unit priorities may require Commanders and Command Sergeant Majors to move Sergeants prior to meeting this requirement. Assignments in Operational Army units as a Team/Squad Leader, Supply NCO, Property Book NCO, Unit Supply Specialist, and Logistics Advisor.', '0bb53645a9a3cd41edfd72e1a3c0c1fa19a3e80866fa9aa705bca11c357b0b9e', 39, 39, null, 301, null, null, false, null),
  ('07f22648-1493-527c-9f87-f2ae730ec620', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'Sergeants selected for TDA gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These tours should be limited to one (1) three-year tour, with the exception of those personnel required to complete a broadening tour in support of Army requirements. TDA assignments include Drill Sergeant, Instructor, Supply Sergeant, Property Book NCO, Supply Technician, Billeting NCO, Asst Sup SGT, Logistics & Supply NCO, TSF NCO, Property Book Manager, Armorer, Supply Specialist, Mil Clerk OAB, SA Ground Logistics, Logistic Specialist, Log NCOIC (J4), Unit Armorer, Property MGMT NCO, SR Supply SGT, TNG MGT NCO, and OPNS SGT.', 'c1a1ad8913d4670ea0136f149d086f177cf7048ad5aa65c80ee080c41e50c18a', 39, 39, null, 302, null, null, false, null),
  ('9df8e968-74aa-585e-882d-60b8062d5ac5', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to chapter 3; Army Career Tracker (ACT) at https://actnow.army.mil; TC 7-22.7; Army Training Information System (ATIS) at https://www.pdmatis.army.mil/.', '7345beb1d9eab7bc9ff4d40e11cfed7f7dc794420c71074b13e9a2d06abd0275', 39, 39, null, 303, null, null, false, null),
  ('3c426493-7de8-5a8b-8ba4-4e3a0fbdc145', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'Airborne, Jumpmaster, GCSS-Army Material Managers Course, Contracting Officer Representative (COR), Master Fitness Trainer, Enlisted Aide Training Course, Master Resiliency Trainer, Equal Opportunity Course, Air Assault, Ranger, and Unit NBC Course.
(d) Special assignments. 1) Broadening Assignments: Recruiter, Enlisted Aide, Defense Attache, and Drill Sergeant. 2) MOS Enhancing: Security Force Assistance Brigade (SFAB) or any Special Operations assignment, White House Communication Agency (WHCA).', '637581674a754338b18745685b37916e9fa69f9460624298dadc2836dad4d7b3', 39, 39, null, 304, null, null, false, null),
  ('7e2ff827-7ecd-51d7-bd39-9d38e41b8d38', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'SLC and Reclassification.', '89465a136a1bc1d444b6ef3a5cb30f668f135a6ec2e7ca121e3e36965ce77e32', 39, 39, null, 305, null, null, false, null),
  ('8ff68bfb-ffb5-5ba1-9325-8f92ac7f7d79', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 28. MOS 92Y Unit Supply Specialist', 'The critical developmental assignment for an MOS 92Y Staff Sergeant as a Squad Leader or Supply Sergeant for 24 months or serving on staff for 24 months. Although the proponent recommends all MOS 92Y Staff Sergeants serve a minimum of 24 months as a Squad Leader or Section Sergeant prior to being assigned to other leadership duties in operational units, unit strengths, operational requirements, and unit priorities may require Commanders and Command Sergeant Majors to move Staff Sergeants prior to meeting this requirement. Assignments in Operational Army units as a, Supply Sergeant, Senior Supply Sergeant, Logistics Advisor, Property Book NCO, S4 NCOIC.', 'ae8d3af3d4fe353a5e173946a5161b3ebd3bde47aa22589a963fe1173cdeab4e', 39, 40, null, 306, null, null, false, null),
